from pathlib import Path
import base64, html, json, hashlib, subprocess
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
out=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
chapters=[
("01","Raw clay: first material checkpoint","a8f0bf6","raw-clay-checkpoint-1","Regular rings and a uniform surface needed material detail. Original normal and roughness maps added irregular throwing marks, grain and quiet mottling. This was a first pass, not the final texture.",[("before-desktop-close.png","Before: uniform surface"),("after-desktop-close.png","After: first procedural raw surface")]),
("02","Lighting: give surfaces something to reflect","afecc45","lighting-checkpoint-2","A soft studio environment, warm key light and approximate cavity shading improved depth and reflection cues. The environment was generated originally; no reference photographs became textures.",[("before-fired-close.png","Before: fired surface"),("after-fired-close.png","After: environment reflections")]),
("03","Glaze: make final firing visible","4bb5cd0","glaze-checkpoint-3","Unfired glaze stays chalky and matte. Final firing reveals richer color, a clear coat and reflections. Reversed rim and floor triangle winding also caused the dark lid-like rim and was corrected.",[("after-desktop-glazed-close.png","Same checkpoint: unfinished glaze"),("after-desktop-fired-close.png","Same checkpoint: after final firing")]),
("04","Rim and interior: soften the transition","a9d628d","walls-checkpoint-4","A rounded lip and continuous inner shading replaced a flat bridge and abrupt floor shading. Existing wall-thickness guards remained; the change did not force every vessel to have thinner walls.",[("before-desktop-raw-close.png","Before: rim transition"),("after-desktop-raw-close.png","After: rounded lip")]),
("05","Look again: refine the raw surface","ab0139c","raw-clay-reference-review","Video comparison exposed three differences: broad blurred marks, overly sandy relief and stretched rim texture. Finer circular lines, sparse pores and separate raw rim coordinates addressed those differences. References were visual research only, never runtime textures.",[("before-desktop-close.png","Before: first material system"),("after-desktop-close.png","After: reference-driven refinement")]),
("06","Tools: recovery with limits","8973c9b","sponge-tool-review","Sponge can remove shallow marks, while deep cuts retain at least 70% of their original depth. Repeated contact preserves that protection instead of restarting the allowance. This is an intentional simulation limit, not a claim of literal wet-clay physics.",[("1280-before.png","Before sponge contact"),("1280-after.png","After bounded smoothing")]),
("07","Needle and motion: detail without another main tool","4c6f4e3 / c0f454d","needle-motion-review","Needle lives within Carve for shallow incisions. Raw micro-relief becomes quieter as wheel speed increases and returns when the wheel slows. This is contrast reduction, not true motion blur.",[("1280-needle.png","Needle incision checkpoint"),("1280-stopped-close.png","Stopped: stronger relief"),("1280-fast-close.png","Fast: quieter relief")]),
("08","The failed dog bowl: a useful test","2736f84","dog-bowl-attempt","Trying normal controls produced a squat vase with a thick shoulder rather than the intended open dog bowl. Opening depth and disconnected inner/outer shaping were limiting the outcome. Preserve this failed attempt: it explains why the next change mattered.",[("05-finished-raw.png","Actual failed attempt—not a target rendering")]),
("09","Redo: connected opening, then a cylinder","170681b","connected-cylinder-review","Opening depth now follows available body height above a protected floor; widening the hollow moves the outer wall, and an upward Hands pull raises connected walls. The desktop bowl reached an opening radius of 1.28 and depth of 0.811; the next pull raised height from 1.119 to 1.494 (scene units).",[("1280-05-finished-raw.png","Redo: open bowl"),("1280-06-cylinder.png","Next gesture: upright cylinder"),("390-05-finished-raw.png","Phone-layout bowl"),("390-06-cylinder.png","Phone-layout cylinder")])
]
css="body{margin:0;background:#eee7da;color:#302a24;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:48px 24px}h1{font:56px/1.05 Georgia;max-width:850px}h2{font:32px/1.2 Georgia}section{padding:32px 0;border-top:1px solid #bcb09c}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px}figure{margin:0;background:#fffaf1;padding:12px}img{width:100%;height:400px;object-fit:contain;background:#e6dac6}figcaption{font-size:15px;padding:10px 4px}.meta{font-size:14px;color:#665744}.note{padding:20px;background:#ded1bc}a{color:#76502e}@media(max-width:650px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:38px}}"
parts=[f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Virtual Clay Studio — Material to Making</title><style>{css}</style><main><p>VIRTUAL CLAY STUDIO · MILESTONE JOURNAL · OCTOBER 16, 2026</p><h1>From believable clay to a bowl you can actually make</h1><p>A curated progression through local checkpoints, a failed attempt and the cylinder redo. Snapshot: <b>170681b</b>. These prototypes are local, not a record of deployed production.</p><p class="note">Archive rule: every meaningful checkpoint stays in Git, with complete evidence under docs/. Drive contains milestone-level screenshots, guides, reviews and handoffs only. This review embeds selected original screenshots so it remains readable offline.</p>']
manifest=[]
for num,title,commit,folder,body,images in chapters:
 parts.append(f'<section><p class="meta">{num} · {html.escape(commit)} · docs/{folder}/</p><h2>{title}</h2><p>{body}</p><div class="grid">')
 for name,caption in images:
  p=root/'docs'/folder/name
  data=p.read_bytes()
  manifest.append(dict(path=str(p.relative_to(root)),caption=caption,sha256=hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()))
  parts.append(f'<figure><img alt="{html.escape(caption)}" src="data:image/png;base64,{base64.b64encode(data).decode()}"><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>')
 parts.append('</div></section>')
parts.append('<section><h2>What the tests do—and do not—establish</h2><p>Eight Node suites and browser checks were recorded for the connected-wall milestone. Browser layouts covered 320, 390, 430 and 1280 pixels. Phone opening and pulling used CDP touch at 4× CPU throttling; initial preparation used keyboard input and finishing used mouse input. This is not physical-phone testing or a novice usability study.</p><p class="note"><b>Still unresolved:</b> a held-Sponge sample at 390px/4× CPU measured median 16.7ms but p95 150ms. Intermittent geometry-update stutter needs profiling before release. Fired material runs measured around 30fps; do not describe all stages as 60fps.</p><h2>Continue the history</h2><p>Full screenshots, review pages, scripts and measurements remain in each named docs/ directory. DECISIONS.md records technical rationale. Earlier Drive case studies remain historical records; this milestone review does not replace them.</p><p><a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/11RVmXTlLYvRyzMkDwmnvEvfFI0Yz_hAL">Project journal and pictures</a> · <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tL8QNoQNmV23eYQ135R7Mtd7mQGJErFw956vp6pQ7hs/edit">Earlier master case study</a></p></section></main></html>')
(out/'review.html').write_text(''.join(parts))
(out/'selected-evidence.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2)+'\n')
tracked=subprocess.check_output(['git','ls-files','docs'],cwd=root,text=True).splitlines()
(out/'README.md').write_text("# Material to making — milestone archive\n\nSnapshot 170681b; curated October 16, 2026. Open review.html for the ordered visual story.\n\nArchive policy: preserve every meaningful checkpoint in Git and review evidence under docs/. Only milestone-level screenshots, guides, reviews and handoffs go to Drive. Do not upload every test capture or scratch file.\n\nThe self-contained review embeds "+str(len(manifest))+" selected screenshots. selected-evidence.json records original paths and SHA-256 hashes; originals remain in their checkpoint directories. build.py reproduces the review.\n\nExisting Drive journal: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/11RVmXTlLYvRyzMkDwmnvEvfFI0Yz_hAL\nMilestone destination: 03 — Handoffs + checkpoints.\n\nKnown limitation: held-Sponge mobile-proxy p95 150ms; no real-device verification. Nothing deployed.\n")
print(f'{len(manifest)} selected screenshots; review { (out/"review.html").stat().st_size:,} bytes; {len(tracked)} tracked docs files')
